how do i add more posts to the site
Thought: The user wants to know how to add more posts to their Hugo site. I should explain the process clearly:
1. Create a new Markdown file in content/posts/
2. Use the frontmatter format (title, date, slug, tags, aliases, featureimage)
3. Write the content in Markdown or HTML
4. Build/deploy
I should also mention they can use the import script if they have more Blogger exports, or manually create files.
Two options:
1. Manual (new post)
Create a .md file in content/posts/:
---
title: "Your Post Title"
date: 2024-05-21T10:00:00
slug: "your-post-slug"
tags:
  - Guide
  - Bannerlord
aliases:
  - /2024/05/your-post-title.html
featureimage: "https://example.com/image.jpg"
---
Your post content here. Markdown or HTML both work.
2. Bulk import (more Blogger exports)
If you have another Google Takeout feed.atom:
python3 scripts/import-blogger.py path/to/feed.atom content/posts/
Then commit and push — GitHub Actions will auto-deploy:
git add content/posts/ && git commit -m "Add new posts" && git push
